{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life","id":1492980,"title":"[M20] Entropy Sphere (partially) substituting Life?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-13T09:04:58-07:00","id":1492980,"title":"[M20] Entropy Sphere (partially) substituting Life?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> The M20 write up mentions that Entropy 4 can be used to cause or <b>heal</b> aggravated damage. Assuming a Paradigm that permits it: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does it require other Spheres (Life, Spirit, Matter), or it does this on its own? Both for damage and healing.</li> <li>Could it cause/heal lethal/bashing also?</li> <li>On its own (no other Sphere needed), what other capabilities from the Life Sphere (if any) could it replicate?</li> <li>Reattaching limbs?</li> <li>Regrowing limbs?</li> <li>Kill virii/bacteria?</li> <li>Revert localized damage? (Burns, lacerations, etc)</li> </ol><br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-13-2022, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T19:04:56-07:00","id":1493039,"title":"","content":"I'll talk mostly from memory of another thread where we discussed precisely that:<br /> <br /> 1 - Since it is stated directly and with no caveats in the description of level 4, I'd say it needs no other sphere;<br /> <br /> 2 - Probably, I don't see why not. The ST would be justified in imposing this limit, though, simply because the rules are silent on the matter;<br /> <br /> 3 - None. By itself it would just be governing systemic collapse;<br /> <br /> Damage is an abstraction and an organism is a system, those are the key concepts to understand damage/healing through Entropy. You don't die exactly because of trauma, loss of blood or infection. You die because at one point the whole system could keep itself despite failures and at another point it couldn't. And since every system isn't a thing in itself, but an emerging feature of the interaction between parts, this is rather hard to really predict. That's why sometimes people survive freak accidents and sometimes they die of getting up too fast, death is a systemic collapse.<br /> <br /> So what is Damage? It is an abstraction of how close you are to the event that will cause a systemic collapse. What kills you isn't the damage, it is the last damaging event. What hinders you isn't pain necessarily, but how much the last damaging events hindered the functionality of the system. How Entropy affects that at level 4? It affects the very governing force behind any systemic failure: yours truly, entropy itself.<br /> <br /> How does it looks like? Well, how does someone looks like when the doctors say they're out of danger? Missing limbs are still missing, gaping wounds are still gaping, but the body managed. Your body managed to stop blood loss, things are just as bad as before, but you're stable, you'll be fine. Your life hangs on luck alone, but luck is on your side, it seems. The building withstood heavy damage, but refuses to cease to be a building, the box was shaken by an earthquake, but the contents refused to mix or break, your body is in a terrible shape, but it just won't stop working. Because at the end, the transition from being to not being is entropy.<br /> <br /> One important aspect to it, though: contrary to Life, an Entropy healing effect isn't necessarily lasting by default. It may be powerful, but still be a temporary, or even permanent but dismissible. Let this sink and enjoy toying with the distinction between using one or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T04:41:32-07:00","id":1493055,"title":"","content":"My original answer was lost so I'm going to retry.<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does it require other Spheres (Life, Spirit, Matter), or it does this on its own? Both for damage and healing.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">No. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, Entropy is given this ability with no restrictions. While M20 can trip itself up in the requirements section this time it tracks. Entropy is a sphere that can target patterns and this effect explicitly does, so there shouldn't be targeting spheres. You also don't need to anchor the spell to a pattern in this case.</div></li> <li>Could it cause/heal lethal/bashing also?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Trickier. The reason that Entropy causes aggravated damage is that it attacks the pattern directly. It isn't spelled out as explicitly as it could be but pattern damage is aggravated damage and vice versa. I'm inclined to say you can't use Entropy directly on a pattern and not cause aggravated damage. That said, there are other ways of attacking with entropy and the writeup does indicate that Entropy 4 can affect living bodies. While you will probably not run across a situation where it matters, that is a different effect.<br /> <br /> The distinction might matter with healing, though, as you'd need two different spells to heal both Agg and other damage.</div></li> <li>On its own (no other Sphere needed), what other capabilities from the Life Sphere (if any) could it replicate?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Very little. The effect isn't described as a graceful or nuanced, it is just increasing or decreasing the entropy in the pattern. There's nothing to indicate fine control.</div></li> <li>Reattaching limbs?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Maybe. Just maybe. f it is a perfectly clean cut and you put the limb in place precisely. Otherwise no.</div></li> <li>Regrowing limbs?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">No. Human bodies don't normally grow back limbs so you can't induce them to with Entropy.</div></li> <li>Kill virii/bacteria?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yes. </div></li> <li>Revert localized damage? (Burns, lacerations, etc)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Yes. If you get into the details, you probably couldn't target a specific wound. I don't think you need to get that granular at the table. </div></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T17:34:29-07:00","id":1493085,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T23:34:18-07:00","id":1493098,"title":"","content":"A small thought on the relevance of patterns to Entropy. As far as I can tell the concept of a pattern derives from the Platonic theory of forms (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theory_of_forms\" target=\"_blank\">Theory of forms - Wikipedia</a>) and so the form of a body represents the ideal essence, or perfection of that form. Thus, the pattern is the perfect form of the body, i.e. undamaged and in perfect working order.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 has the ability to directly affect body patterns either increasing or decreasing the entropy within the pattern, and this it's 'perfection'. This change to the pattern is reflected as damage (increased pattern entropy) or healing (decreased pattern entropy) to the body.<br /> <br /> As a different example, imagine a photograph of a person, the original photo shows them in great health, but increasing entropy is like making a copy of a copy over and over again, so that eventually the picture is nothing but a smudge. That's how increasing entropy in a pattern damages it, by making the pattern less and less perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 09-15-2022, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T12:01:03-07:00","id":1493123,"title":"","content":"I would have to disagree with my friends above in that Entropy 4 cannot be used to kind of replicate other uses of Life; I believe it can, albeit in a much more subtle, harder and less effective way, or at least in a much longer span of time to manifest, and a bit more restricted way.<br /> <br /> In order to try to understand why, we must first ubderstand what Entropy is and does (the Sphere, not the real life physics meaning).<br /> <br /> I always like to compare Entropy with Spirit, because Spirit is the most &quot;mystic&quot; of the Spheres, so in order to understand Spirit under techno paradigms - &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; - we must first understand it in a mystical sense to only then &quot;translate&quot; it to whatever technobabble desired.<br /> <br /> With Entropy, the reverse is true, so it's easier to understand it using real life scientific concepts and after that &quot;translate&quot; those to a coherent mystical view.<br /> <br /> What's important to know is that such &quot;translations&quot; are for us players and STs to understand them out of character, and they do not occur in the game universe.<br /> <br /> Now, Entropy, in my experience, is the most misunderstood of the Spheres, even more so than Prime or Spirit. With that being said, we gotta ask, what is Entropy? What exactly does it control?<br /> <br /> Well, it's chance, probability. Or, destiny and fate.<br /> <br /> So, the first thing we must understand is that it doesnt control ANYTHING directly, but rather the &quot;randomness&quot; (if there is such a thing) all around us.<br /> <br /> How does a living body act? How does it work?<br /> <br /> When a molecule of oxigen is &quot;captured&quot; by a hemoglobine, how does that work?<br /> <br /> Well, in real life, it certanly isnt &quot;magic&quot;. The hemoglobine in fact have an electromagnetic affinity towards a molecule of O2, thus when they happen to be in close proximity, the hemoglobine &quot;captures&quot; it, like a magnet attracs an iron nail.<br /> <br /> The thing is thou, both the hemoglobines and the O2 are RANDOMLY distributed over the body. See where this is going?<br /> <br /> The use of Entropy does NOT make the Hemoglobines magically transmutate into something else, but rather you control the <b>random distribution of hemoglobines in the blood</b>.<br /> <br /> Take that example and apply it to almost all molecular biochemistry happening in the body. For example, our DNA produces RNA by bounding with the building blocks bases present in our citoplasm, and those bound with aminoacids to form proteins. I wont describe the entire process because that would be tedius, but suffice is to say that those RNA and aminoacids molecules are &quot;randomly&quot; &quot;floating&quot; inside the cell. Now, our biochemistry have several catalyzers to speed up all those processes, a consequence of billions of years of evolution to optimize our processes, but all of those still act upon molecules randomly floating inside the cells.<br /> <br /> And here is where Entropy acts: actively driving all the random processes in a specific direction.<br /> <br /> Now, pushing a single molecule of O2 towards an hemoglobine 0,001 seconds faster wont make much of a difference, but if by &quot;pure luck&quot; (aka Entropy effect) you make EVERY single O2 molecule position itself in a more &quot;favorable&quot; way to be more easily captured, having every single aminoacid in the body be in a more optimized position by pure &quot;random luck&quot; in order to have just a tiny little edge in the protein syntetization inside the cells, and have every single cells of the immune system just fall in line, having that exact immune cell be in the exact place where an infectious virus just entered the body... Every single one of those tiny changes, by themselves, have a completely null impact.<br /> <br /> However, ALL of those changing at the same time have a MASSIVE impact.<br /> <br /> Thus, could you use Entropy 4 for example to create an effect similar to the vampiric discipline Potency - there is, add extra damage to a punch?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, YES. The effect will have every single muscular fiber in your body move in the perfect way to maximize impact; every molecule of adrenaline hit the muscular cells in an optimized way; the very biophysics movement of your body to be optimized, and when you hit your target, instead of breaking your own hand, the energy gets dispersed in your fist due to many &quot;random&quot; events, like the angle, the fact that some additional fat was delivered by your blood to your hand in that exactly moment by &quot;sheer luck&quot;, and another huge array of random tiny events that are imperceptible by themselves, but pile up upon each other to cause a massive emergent pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T12:41:52-07:00","id":1493125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493123#post1493123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> Thus, could you use Entropy 4 for example to create an effect similar to the vampiric discipline Potency - there is, add extra damage to a punch?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, YES</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree with this approach on several grounds. Firstly, it's using real world science to justify in-game sphere creep. The game is all about paradigms and allowing science to be the 'best' paradigm, because we can use real world knowledge to back it up is a fundamentally bd approach to playing the game - well unless it's a pure technocracy game of course.<br /> <br /> Secondly, even with a suitable in-game paradigm, the amount of randomness that needs to be redirected is phenomenal, way beyond any sort of reasonable probability. As an ST I'd be highly dubious if a player came up with this justification, enough that I wouldn't be interested in playing with that player again.<br /> <br /> Lastly allowing spheres' range of effects to creep too far into one another is taking steps down the road to power gaming hell. I'm sure we've all seen the 'Spirit can do anything' approach to Mage and hopefully realised why it's such a bad idea. There has to be balance between the spheres' capabilities or the game devolves into who can come up with the must dubious bullshit for justifying their spellcasting, which, if you want to play it like that is fine for you, but I don't want anything to do with it, and it's not polite to try to pass it off as standard game play.<br /> <br /> p.s. I forgot all about the 'Optional Rule: Minimum Abilities' (M20, p276) and 'Dude, Do You Even Know What You\u2019re Doing?' (HDYDT?, p28) - even with the right paradigm it would take a very highly skilled character to understand all the concepts, biochemistry, and math needed to accomplish this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 09-15-2022, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T12:42:46-07:00","id":1493126,"title":"","content":"Now, can Entropy 2 be used to create a hurricane, for example?<br /> <br /> Well... YES!<br /> <br /> Now, creating a hurricane with Entropy 2 would be a MASSIVE endeavor - meaning, requiring a TON of sucesses.<br /> <br /> Why? Because, unlike using Forces to &quot;force&quot; the air into a massive kinetic force, as if the Mage became a massive magnet capable of attracting a huge mass of air molecules, doing this using Entropy 2 means that you are changing the random movement of each air molecule around in such a way that those pile up upon one another until they reach an apex on a huge <b>Butterfly Effect</b>.<br /> <br /> How likely would that be to occur?<br /> <br /> Well, in one place it may be very simple. Maybe there's already a hot air mass in collision course with a cold air mass, so changing just a few molecules can start the &quot;domino effect&quot; that would culminate in a chain reaction, unleashing a hurricane. In the Caribbean for example, that may be easily done, not requiring that many successes.<br /> <br /> Here in Brazil, that simply NEVER happens - so it would truly require some exceptional collection of &quot;random amount of events&quot; to trigger it.<br /> <br /> Lets put it on numbers: lets say that in a single moment, there's a 1 in 100 chance in a region of the Caribbean that a hurricane could spontaneously form.<br /> <br /> Well, that's a probability... Which is EXACTLY the purview of Entropy.<br /> <br /> So, just change the chances, get your desired effect.<br /> <br /> So, maybe in this case you &quot;only&quot; need 10 successes with Entropy 2.<br /> <br /> Now, in the case of Brazil, lets say that the chance is 1 in a million. Not impossible, just highly unlikely.<br /> <br /> So, now you'll need a much greater set of improbable events to kick this off; the ST could say you need 10.000 successes for this (!). Or, more generously, instead of a linear escale of successes towards probability, say that this is a somewhat exponential or logarithmic scale, so say, 20 or 30 or 50 successes for pulling that one off.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there are some things that are just outright &quot;impossible&quot; for Entropy 3, or just simply so unlikely to be virtually impossible. Can Oxigen naturally transmute into Hidrogen?<br /> <br /> Well, the chance is close to zero... Or near so. In fact, given an infinite amount of time... It could. But that would only occur under quantic fluctuations, so it's so ridiculously low that I would require 1 TRILLION successes to change O2 into H2 using Entropy 3 alone.<br /> <br /> Thus, while theoretically possible, it is impossible in practical terms.<br /> <br /> Likewise, let us imagine for a moment DNA mutations. Let us put mystical interpretations aside for a moment and stick to hard science for a moment.<br /> <br /> Now, a bird's wing is codified in their DNA.<br /> <br /> It is possible to thinker with human DNA to create humans with wings.<br /> <br /> So, what's the chances of thinkering with human DNA in order to create humans with functional wings?<br /> <br /> Well, it's very, very low. Could be done, but highly unlikely.<br /> <br /> Most of the times, DNA mutations cause CANCER, or genetic diseases when not cancer.<br /> <br /> Once upon a time thou, such mutations actually breed some improvements to the organism.<br /> <br /> Those are absolutely random - thus within the purview of Entropy.<br /> <br /> So, using Entropy 4 to make someone faster or stronger is relatively easy... Growing wings spontaneously just by chance manipulation could well be in the realm of needing BILLIONS of successes however.<br /> <br /> But, inducing cancer or a heart attack would be very, very simple.<br /> <br /> In here, I'll use an example from Mage, Revised edition for Entropy 4: Blessing. With it, you could bless an unborn fetus with good health. That's a relatively easy thing to do - you just increase the chances that the body will develop in the most optimal way.<br /> <br /> This example also proves in an official sense that Entropy 4 CAN indeed be used to alter live patterns besides just harm/heal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T13:14:38-07:00","id":1493128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493125#post1493125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to disagree with this approach on several grounds. Firstly, it's using real world science to justify in-game sphere creep. The game is all about paradigms and allowing science to be the 'best' paradigm, because we can use real world knowledge to back it up is a fundamentally bd approach to playing the game - well unless it's a pure technocracy game of course.<br /> <br /> Secondly, even with a suitable in-game paradigm, the amount of randomness that needs to be redirected is phenomenal, way beyond any sort of reasonable probability. As an ST I'd be highly dubious if a player came up with this justification, enough that I wouldn't be interested in playing with that player again.<br /> <br /> Lastly allowing spheres' range of effects to creep too far into one another is taking steps down the road to power gaming hell. I'm sure we've all seen the 'Spirit can do anything' approach to Mage and hopefully realised why it's such a bad idea. There has to be balance between the spheres' capabilities or the game devolves into who can come up with the must dubious bullshit for justifying their spellcasting, which, if you want to play it like that is fine for you, but I don't want anything to do with it, and it's not polite to try to pass it off as standard game play.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think this view is &quot;creeping too far into one another&quot;, then Im not being able to properly communicate exactly my meaning.<br /> <br /> Also, as I stated in my last post, which came after your reply, I know from memory that at least in Revised there's an example that proves my point to be correct. I cant cite other editions because, althought Im familiar with them all, Im most familiar with revised, and I know for sure that it is there, and I recall it from memory (bah, Im too lazy to look it all up for the sake of the argument thou).<br /> <br /> In there, in fact it even states that you CAN <b>induce specific traits</b> while giving your &quot;bless&quot; - therefore, you could for example determine the color of the eyes, the tone of the skin, or even make the baby be above the average in intelligence, strenght, speed etc etc, but that since those specific traits are HARDER (aka there are lower CHANCES) to do for the person's entire life, what the Mage most usually do is simply insure that the baby will develop healthly and free of diseases; that however, does NOT mean that the baby's &quot;fairy&quot; cant induce specific changes. It can.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;you are making Scientific Paradigm become more 'true' than others&quot;, you are greatly misunderstanding me:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What's important to know is that such &quot;translations&quot; are for us players and STs to understand them out of character, and they do not occur in the game universe.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>When a person is firstly introduced to Mage, when it is time to explain the &quot;Spirit worlds&quot;, we use &quot;Avatar&quot;, &quot;Spirits&quot; and &quot;Ephemera&quot; to explain it.<br /> <br /> That doesnt mean that all the technobabble about &quot;Antropic Fields&quot; or &quot;Parallel Dimensions&quot; are less true or less valid than &quot;Spirits&quot;, just that it is easier to explain to the PLAYERS what a &quot;Parallel Dimension&quot; is in the setting once they managed to understand what &quot;Spirit World&quot; is.<br /> <br /> Likewise, just because Im using &quot;quantum fluctuations&quot; to EXEMPLIFY how Entropy works and thus make it easier to digest for the PLAYERS, and easier to visualize, it doesnt mean that it overrides or overules the in game Paradigms of &quot;Fortune Manipulation&quot; or &quot;Supplicate for Divine Intervention&quot;. <br /> <br /> All are still equally valid in game, but it just means that it would be harder to explain for us real world non Mages the limits of this fictional &quot;superpower&quot; by trying to explain it in terms of the intervention of the divine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T21:43:43-07:00","id":1493149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493123#post1493123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Entropy, in my experience, is the most misunderstood of the Spheres, even more so than Prime or Spirit. With that being said, we gotta ask, what is Entropy? What exactly does it control?<br /> <br /> Well, it's chance, probability. Or, destiny and fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. Not irl.<br /> <br /> Entropy is a complicated concept. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entropy\" target=\"_blank\">Complicated like Hell</a>. But it relates to probability and chance only in a tangential (although relevant) way. It actually has far more relationship with this in the game than in real science (science, because it is an important element in too many areas beyond physics, despite being developed in thermodynamics).<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, you can affect probability with Entropy, but it is just one aspect in or out of the game, that gives you only a very limited understanding of it. It has also a lot to do with the relationship between a system macro and micro states (how the observable state of a system relates to its infinite component parts), the spread of energy within a system given it observable parameters, the amount of useful energy within a system in contrast to total energy, the amount of information and many other things.<br /> <br /> That's why Entropy is considered an \u00dcber Sphere by many players. Because it can translate itself into many seemingly distinct things that have little to do with each other in game terms (in real life they do have a relationship that can be mathematically and experimentally demonstrated, like how a decrease in entropy of <i>information</i> demonstrably produces <i>heat</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493123#post1493123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have to disagree with my friends above in that Entropy 4 cannot be used to kind of replicate other uses of Life; I believe it can, albeit in a much more subtle, harder and less effective way, or at least in a much longer span of time to manifest, and a bit more restricted way.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the above said, though, changes little in regards to your position, although it has other problems.<br /> <br /> First, your proposal is technically correct, but effectively unfeasible. You're only pointing to the fact that one can <i>theoretically</i> cause anything to happen with sufficient probability control. It is a valid thought experiment with a character that can achieve any arbitrarily high amount of successes. But when we discuss what a Sphere can do, it is usually about what it can do within its usual purview, not in extreme cases. You'll get another reaction from others entirely if you just say that Entropy can do that <i>in extreme cases</i>. This is the distinction you're failing to convey.<br /> <br /> Second, it still misses some points in terms of stating context, the reason why the passage you cited doesn't seems to really help your case. A Mage that blesses a child, or an adult going to start an exercise regimen, can indeed and within reason affect their future stats. But that isn't Entropy boosting their Life Pattern, A.K.A. giving a bonus, and instead it affecting the chances of a given <i><b>natural</b></i> outcome of the process. The distinction is between what you can do for someone years before a battle or just seconds before.<br /> <br /> Using Entropy to affect the outcome of a natural process through time is a different animal from using it to <b>cause</b> the same effect as another Sphere, because by stating the later you're not only saying that it can eventually cause a similar change, you're saying that it causes a similar change in a similar way under similar conditions. Not identical, but reasonably similar. The similarity you're actually alluding to isn't reasonable, it is <i>extremo situ</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T22:15:09-07:00","id":1493197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493149#post1493149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't. Not irl.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I had stated that I was specifically talking about the Mage Sphere of Entropy, not the real life concept of Entropy in physics science, but in case I wasnt clear, now I rectify myself: this is what I meant. It's not what the real life physics concept, but the Mage Sphere.<br /> <br /> Hence why this is also called as the <i>Fortuna</i> (fortune/destiny in latim) Sphere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monsteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, your proposal is technically correct, but effectively unfeasible. You're only pointing to the fact that one can theoretically cause anything to happen with sufficient probability control. It is a valid thought experiment with a character that can achieve any arbitrarily high amount of successes. But when we discuss what a Sphere can do, it is usually about what it can do within its usual purview, not in extreme cases. You'll get another reaction from others entirely if you just say that Entropy can do that in extreme cases. This is the distinction you're failing to convey.<br /> <br /> Second, it still misses some points in terms of stating context, the reason why the passage you cited doesn't seems to really help your case. A Mage that blesses a child, or an adult going to start an exercise regimen, can indeed and within reason affect their future stats. But that isn't Entropy boosting their Life Pattern, A.K.A. giving a bonus, and instead it affecting the chances of a given natural outcome of the process. The distinction is between what you can do for someone years before a battle or just seconds before.<br /> <br /> Using Entropy to affect the outcome of a natural process through time is a different animal from using it to cause the same effect as another Sphere, because by stating the later you're not only saying that it can eventually cause a similar change, you're saying that it causes a similar change in a similar way under similar conditions. Not identical, but reasonably similar. The similarity you're actually alluding to isn't reasonable, it is extremo situ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, absolutely. I said I still had to expand my answer. Indeed you're right. An Entropy 4 effect to make someone suffer a heart attack could strike the target in a few seconds in the case of a morbid obese person, or someone who already suffers some heart condition, or it could take 10 years to fulfill in an olympic athlete, adjusted by successes.<br /> <br /> I'd say that any of those would rely heavily on the subjective judgment of the ST; still, while anything is <i>theoretically</i> possible, most of the truly outrageous effects would become virtually impossible - like requiring 1 billion successes to grow functional wings, or 1 million successes, since that in practical terms there's no difference between those.<br /> <br /> Yes, I absolutely agree.<br /> <br /> But the purpose of my thought experiment is not to make a list of exactly how ridiculously each extreme possibility is unlikely is how big of &quot;virtually impossible&quot; each one is, like saying that &quot;wings is 1 million successes impossible, turning someone into a frog is 1 billion successes impossible, turning into a dragon is 1 trillion successes impossible&quot; and so on, but rather to try to understand what the limits of the Entropy Sphere are and thus what IS feasible.<br /> <br /> Like an example that I cited above, but I'll expand a bit here.<br /> <br /> The vampiric disciplines Potence and Fortitude.<br /> <br /> In my tabletops, I made it so that those are emulated by using Entropy 4, and NOT using Life.<br /> <br /> And my reasoning: those vampiric disciplines are the result of the &quot;magic&quot; of the cursed bodies of the bloodsuckers. It is NOT the result of muscular or bone mass. Thus, they are not caused by some special life modification.<br /> <br /> Life can increase dots in physical attributes, but Entropy 4 can be used to give a &quot;boost&quot; to those natural aptitudes that goes beyond what the natural biophysics of the body could, in a similar fashion as Potence or Fortitude do to vampires.<br /> <br /> Now, this is one thing that I consider to be in the realm of the feasible for Entropy 4.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think it's important to understand exactly the full array of what's possible for Entropy and inside that, what's feasible and what's not.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I fully agree with you, I just hope I've managed to made my point a bit more clear; I'll admit, sometimes Im super confusing, things seem to make sense in my head, but when I communicate my &quot;super clear&quot; messages, nobody but me understands lol, so if there's still some doubt, please ask away and I'll try to explain in some other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T22:38:09-07:00","id":1493198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493149#post1493149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Entropy to affect the outcome of a natural process through time is a different animal from using it to <b>cause</b> the same effect as another Sphere, because by stating the later you're not only saying that it can eventually cause a similar change, you're saying that it causes a similar change in a similar way under similar conditions. Not identical, but reasonably similar. The similarity you're actually alluding to isn't reasonable, it is <i>extremo situ</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, this is one important point I wanted to touch on too. Yes, I 100% agree. Most of the changes obtained using Entropy 4 are not instantaneous effects. I mean, it could be (like a heart attack or &quot;miraculous healing&quot;), but most often, those will take some undefined amount of time to see it come to the desired conclusion.<br /> <br /> And here's why it's important to clearly understand what Entropy can and cant do. Entropy is NOT direct control over anything, except the random fluctuations of chance. So, for example, when the doctor says that you only have 30% chance to survive the surgery, you can increase those odds to 99.99%.<br /> <br /> That's VERY different from when someone uses Life to DIRECTLY turn the brain cancer into harmless nutrients.<br /> <br /> Changing thing with Life are instantaneous; even if you turn into a dragon, you do it in a second (as soon as you accumulate enough successes at least).<br /> <br /> Likewise, one could use Entropy 5 to &quot;convince&quot; someone of something. Lets say for example that I decided to use Entropy 5 to make you see the &quot;light&quot; that only Anarcho-Capitalism reveals hahaha.<br /> <br /> Ok, you would become an Ancap.<br /> <br /> <b>Eventually</b><br /> <br /> But that's vastly different from using Mind 4 to do it.<br /> <br /> If I use Mind 4 to &quot;convince&quot; you to be an Ancap, what Im essentially doing is a quick and dirty brainwash.<br /> <br /> &quot;Listen to my voice, you are now under my command... After counting to 3, you'll be an Ancap&quot;<br /> <br /> Bam. Done.<br /> <br /> With Entropy 5 however, there's no such thing. Well, it could be that I amassed an ungodly amount of successes, and you started to think about Anarcho Capitalism for &quot;no specific reason&quot;, &quot;out of the blue&quot;, and something just clicks in the right way inside your head.<br /> <br /> Mostly likely thou, what probably would happen is that you start to date some weird boyfriend/girlfriend, or starts to hang around that group of &quot;subversive mischiefs&quot; new friends, or get a glimpse of a book at the library that caught your eyes for &quot;some reason&quot; (you know, all absolutely &quot;random&quot;, there's no Mage pulling the strings of your Destiny, it's all just pure &quot;happenstance&quot;, no reason for you to be suspicious at all), and somehow this idea begins to grow inside of you, slowly but surely.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those are the pathways of Entropy. Sure, making someone trip with Entropy 2 is very funny and a dirty and quick effect, but the array of possibilities of this Sphere is incredibly vast, althought never as direct and fastas the other Spheres, but probably much more subtle than those too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 09-17-2022, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T01:19:11-07:00","id":1493207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493197#post1493197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe I had stated that I was specifically talking about the Mage Sphere of Entropy, not the real life concept of Entropy in physics science, but in case I wasnt clear, now I rectify myself: this is what I meant. It's not what the real life physics concept, but the Mage Sphere.<br /> <br /> Hence why this is also called as the <i>Fortuna</i> (fortune/destiny in latim) Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context it seemed to be the opposite affirmation, that it was about chance irl.<br /> <br /> But even then, that's not completely it. Entropy in the game is linked to chance, but also to decay and systemic phenomena. It is ill-defined and frequently expected to bring something of the scientific concept with it.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying that as something good. I actually think CoD made the right choice in Mage when they split Entropy into Fate and Death and dropped the more vague aspects that didn't really improved the game, just made the Sphere harder to understand for STs and players alike.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493197#post1493197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vampiric disciplines Potence and Fortitude.<br /> <br /> In my tabletops, I made it so that those are emulated by using Entropy 4, and NOT using Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather use Prime, Matter and/or Forces.<br /> <br /> They are mystical powers, even if static. They're not born out of muscles, but they aren't chance or something to that effect, either. They are blood magic.<br /> <br /> Maybe Fortitude could be an Entropy field that takes energy out of attacks, but Potence would probably work better as a &quot;contact kinesis&quot; power, converting Quint into excess kinetic energy. Life could be used only as a means to deliver a Matter effect into a Life pattern, so you can alter the physical properties of your skin to make up for Fortitude, too, or complement Potency and avoid your ligaments breaking apart from the extra tension.<br /> <br /> Entropy as a means to deliver this effect seems... off. Only justified by the notion that vampires are governed by Entropy, and you're borrowing a vampire power. But you're actually emulating the power in another system entirely, unless you want to curse yourself. I don't think this is properly Entropy.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think it's clear enough to me and I basically agree with you, just thought to help you clarify some things that really weren't clear in your previous posts, giving a very distinct impression from what you intended. I also struggle with this sometimes, and in the past struggled a lot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T21:31:54-07:00","id":1493379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493207#post1493207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather use Prime, Matter and/or Forces.<br /> <br /> They are mystical powers, even if static. They're not born out of muscles, but they aren't chance or something to that effect, either. They are blood magic.<br /> <br /> Maybe Fortitude could be an Entropy field that takes energy out of attacks, but Potence would probably work better as a &amp;quot;contact kinesis&amp;quot; power, converting Quint into excess kinetic energy. Life could be used only as a means to deliver a Matter effect into a Life pattern, so you can alter the physical properties of your skin to make up for Fortitude, too, or complement Potency and avoid your ligaments breaking apart from the extra tension.<br /> <br /> Entropy as a means to deliver this effect seems... off. Only justified by the notion that vampires are governed by Entropy, and you're borrowing a vampire power. But you're actually emulating the power in another system entirely, unless you want to curse yourself. I don't think this is properly Entropy.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I think it's clear enough to me and I basically agree with you, just thought to help you clarify some things that really weren't clear in your previous posts, giving a very distinct impression from what you intended. I also struggle with this sometimes, and in the past struggled a lot more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you use Prime to it?<br /> <br /> Yes, Forces I agree. With Forces you just add a &quot;Kinetic Shield&quot;, to either/and add strenght to a blow, easy lifting something or deflecting damage.<br /> <br /> But why Prime?<br /> <br /> As for Matter... I also dont understand. Why? You could combine probably Matter 4 / Life 3 to turn your skin into metal or something, but I wouldnt count this as a &quot;damage reductor&quot;, but rather as donning a piece of armor.<br /> <br /> Oh, I guess you thought I was trying to emulate some sort of Blood Magic effect. No no, that's not what I meant.<br /> <br /> What I was aiming at was just simply replicating the end results with similar effects - aka extra points of damage for a kick or a punch or extra dice to absorb damage. Just that.<br /> <br /> It's a replication of the mechanics, I just used the examples of the vampiric disciplines for the simplicity to explain said effects, but I see that once again I only brought out further confusion.<br /> <br /> So, to clear it up: I allow successes in an Entropy 4 effect to be used to give extra automatic successes for strenght rolls, or for absorbing damage.<br /> <br /> (Forget Potence and Fortitude, I didnt mean to imply any sort of relation to the power source, just the somewhat similar mechanics)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T18:28:59-07:00","id":1493444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493379#post1493379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you use Prime to it?<br /> <br /> Yes, Forces I agree. With Forces you just add a &quot;Kinetic Shield&quot;, to either/and add strenght to a blow, easy lifting something or deflecting damage.<br /> <br /> But why Prime?<br /> <br /> As for Matter... I also dont understand. Why? You could combine probably Matter 4 / Life 3 to turn your skin into metal or something, but I wouldnt count this as a &quot;damage reductor&quot;, but rather as donning a piece of armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy for the effect of adding actual impetus to a punch in a similar scale to Potence seems very odd, I'm not sold on it in practical terms.<br /> <br /> Forces you got alright, Matter is for the lower level effects. Turning skin, or at least some properties of skin, to a more resilient material could be Life 2/Matter 2 depending on the ST if you do it in a way where you consider that Life is just keeping the problems of this imbuing from manifesting for the duration. Otherwise, Life 3/Matter 2 would do the trick. But the real deal would be to use Matter 5 in this effect, as then you can apply matter directly on skin to change its physical properties at your leisure without changing the actual material. But yeah, it is a little contrived and would only be a thing for a character that wants such an effect but is actually more invested in Matter.<br /> <br /> More importantly, Prime is extremely versatile to &quot;pull stuff out of thin air&quot;. Mage is adamant on most Spheres that Laws of Conservation still apply to some extent, unless you're a Master and sometimes even if. While their combat uses can be emulated with other resources, Potence in particular has non-combat uses that are very impressive and would require a lot of energy. Where do you get the extra energy to turn into kinetic energy?<br /> <br /> Unless you have a source to get this energy from or send it to, Forces itself works better with Prime, so it can be stored/get directly from or into Patterns or even Quintessence. Not necessarily enough to be worth further mechanical effects, not every Prime manipulation will generate or destroy Quint, but with far less unpredictable consequences. It also lets you use &quot;Prime Batteries&quot; of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T17:41:18-07:00","id":1493789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493444#post1493444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entropy for the effect of adding actual impetus to a punch in a similar scale to Potence seems very odd, I'm not sold on it in practical terms.<br /> <br /> Forces you got alright, Matter is for the lower level effects. Turning skin, or at least some properties of skin, to a more resilient material could be Life 2/Matter 2 depending on the ST if you do it in a way where you consider that Life is just keeping the problems of this imbuing from manifesting for the duration. Otherwise, Life 3/Matter 2 would do the trick. But the real deal would be to use Matter 5 in this effect, as then you can apply matter directly on skin to change its physical properties at your leisure without changing the actual material. But yeah, it is a little contrived and would only be a thing for a character that wants such an effect but is actually more invested in Matter.<br /> <br /> More importantly, Prime is extremely versatile to &quot;pull stuff out of thin air&quot;. Mage is adamant on most Spheres that Laws of Conservation still apply to some extent, unless you're a Master and sometimes even if. While their combat uses can be emulated with other resources, Potence in particular has non-combat uses that are very impressive and would require a lot of energy. Where do you get the extra energy to turn into kinetic energy?<br /> <br /> Unless you have a source to get this energy from or send it to, Forces itself works better with Prime, so it can be stored/get directly from or into Patterns or even Quintessence. Not necessarily enough to be worth further mechanical effects, not every Prime manipulation will generate or destroy Quint, but with far less unpredictable consequences. It also lets you use &quot;Prime Batteries&quot; of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it a &quot;Metabolic Boost&quot; if you're a Techie-boy or &quot;Heroic Feat&quot; or some such if you're a Mystic. It works in the same ways as I described above for other Entropy effects, tiny little changes that add up to a massive overall effect.<br /> <br /> For a &quot;Fortitude-like&quot; effect it's even more feasible; instead of the bullet blowing up your heart or &quot;if it were just an inch to left you would've been dead&quot;. It simply creates an &quot;Entropic field&quot; of sorts on your body that allows you to rub off the most spetacular damage sources as just bruises.<br /> <br /> Edit: &quot;Heroic Feat&quot; also plays nicely with the more mystic views of the Sphere, regarding about curses/blessings - &quot;I now bestow upon thee, the strenght of Hercules!&quot;, while &quot;Metabolic Boost&quot; feats nicely for the annoying techno-geeks (&quot;Strenght of Hercules? Nonsense pointy hat! This is just an adrenaline rush! Look, I just published a new article about it in the &quot;Ether today&quot; magazine last week about the influence of gamma-ether-waves on adrenal bodily functions)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 09-26-2022, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T23:19:22-07:00","id":1493955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493789#post1493789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call it a &quot;Metabolic Boost&quot; if you're a Techie-boy or &quot;Heroic Feat&quot; or some such if you're a Mystic. It works in the same ways as I described above for other Entropy effects, tiny little changes that add up to a massive overall effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree that for avoiding damage it works well and easy, it isn't Fortitude. It doesn't look like it and it doesn't necessarily plays like it (although it can, I guess). So while it would do the job, I wouldn't count it as &quot;emulate&quot; Fortitude.<br /> <br /> The same for Potence, but I would go farther. It either requires a huge amount of successes for little effect, or it is stupidly contrived, even more so for real feats of strength instead of just dishing damage. Read again what I said, Potence has non-combat uses. How do you describe little coincidences letting someone to lift a car with one hand and walk around carrying it? Or ripping a metal fence and bending bars barehanded? As much as Potence is magical strength, it is still constant, sustainable strength, not damage.<br /> <br /> So, no. I don't see Entropy emulating those, specially Potence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T07:35:45-07:00","id":1493975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493955#post1493955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that for avoiding damage it works well and easy, it isn't Fortitude. It doesn't look like it and it doesn't necessarily plays like it (although it can, I guess). So while it would do the job, I wouldn't count it as &amp;quot;emulate&amp;quot; Fortitude.<br /> <br /> The same for Potence, but I would go farther. It either requires a huge amount of successes for little effect, or it is stupidly contrived, even more so for real feats of strength instead of just dishing damage. Read again what I said, Potence has non-combat uses. How do you describe little coincidences letting someone to lift a car with one hand and walk around carrying it? Or ripping a metal fence and bending bars barehanded? As much as Potence is magical strength, it is still constant, sustainable strength, not damage.<br /> <br /> So, no. I don't see Entropy emulating those, specially Potence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imho, it's like those old urban legends about mothers lifting cars to save their babies in an &quot;adrenaline rush&quot;. <br /> <br /> Entropy is not direct control, it is indeed a mysterious Sphere that operates at the &quot;Quantum level&quot; or by &quot;pulling the threads of Fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> Entropy 4 is no exception, and it does not exert any sort of control over living patterns, but instead it controls the threads of destiny that influence those living patterns.<br /> <br /> So, how does it work? In the same way that an &quot;Entropic Heal&quot; or entropic damage does: by directing the &quot;random&quot; bodily functions. It's that single muscular cell receiving those adrenaline molecules at the right time, at the right moment. It's that bone tissue having the molecular arrangement in just the proper way to sustain that extra pressure that it wouldnt normally be able to.<br /> <br /> It's an emergent phenomena. To me that's as clear as water because Im an evolutionist biology, so I study molecular evolution, and we can see clearly how tiny changes add up over time in order to create vastly different outcomes. It's also the math behind the Chaos Theory, which would take too long to explain, but it work like this, the famous &quot;butterfly effect&quot;, upon which tiny changes create massive differently results. In Science Fiction, it's the old tale of going to the past at the age of the dinossaurs, smashing a butterfly and with it changing the entire evolutionary history of the planet, upon which humanity never comes to be.<br /> <br /> That's also why I envision the Techies paradigm about &quot;magic&quot; as being a &quot;gentle quantum push&quot;, as I stated in another post, by enacting massive changes simply by learning how to position the electrons in one's own brain in the proper way to ignite such butterfly effects on reality - say, by learning to modulate your own brain waves in tune with the exterior world, you are able to unleash a &quot;domino effect&quot; that allows you to open a &quot;worm-hole&quot; (gate) on Space-Time and some such.<br /> <br /> Emergent patterns are basically the thing that I've trained my mind to see, which is why I see it on EVERYTHING; and the funny thing is, they ARE present in everything. Did you know for example that the equations for molecular markers - the changes that the molecules of organisms suffer over generations of evolution - are the same as organisms populations... But not only that, they are the same for the physics of a cloud... But also for the ECONOMY?<br /> <br /> That's right, market fluctuations operate on the same premisses as a population of rabbits shrinks or grows in a given area... Pretty insane, heh?<br /> <br /> Those emergent patterns are present on the origin of life, on the origin of our intelligence, human societies and the economy are emergent patterns, our bodies, our brains... Everything are emergent patterns. AIs, artificial intelligences, are too. For instance, the best AIs today, like GPT3, have BILLIONS of parameters - which are the result of neural networks, are parameters that the AI &quot;thought&quot; itself... And no human actually knows exactly how they work, and there are mathematical reasons for us to not be able to know how they do what they do (yes, very scary I know). AIs are close to true intelligence, because they already became emergent patterns, rather than mere dumb close ended algorithms.<br /> <br /> The thing about emergent patterns is that they ultimately are a collection of several units, but when organized in the proper way, the end result is vastly different.<br /> <br /> For example, if I were to dissassemble your body down to the molecular level, and then I took all the trillions of Carbon, Oxygen, Nitrogen, Hidrogen, Iron, Magnesium, Calcium, Potassium etc etc etc and all other atoms that form your body, if I took every single one of your atoms, and placed them all in a chamber without missing a single one, that still wouldnt make you emerge from it.<br /> <br /> Because you are more than just the sum of your parts. Your body is more than a collection of atoms or even a collection of cells, but is an emergent pattern that arises from how the architecture of those is organized.<br /> <br /> Likewise, a society is more than just a bunch of individuals, but rather how those individuals are organized and interact.<br /> <br /> That all being said, if you manage to change key points of those emergent patterns, and you may enact MASSIVE changes on the overall end result.<br /> <br /> In nothing this is more clear than for someone that studies molecular evolution; a single molecule change in the DNA can cause a MASSIVE change in the entire organism during reproduction - in most of the cases, this means cancer or other diseases, but even then it's a massive change, and every once in a while it gives a massive fitness advantage.<br /> <br /> Bioengineering, by the way, is the most massive &quot;butterfly effect&quot; of all time. Like, chaging half a dozen of microscopic molecules in order to breed square watermelons. This is like &quot;real life Entropy Sphere&quot; in action.<br /> <br /> Besides, there's nothing more Entropy-like than blessing someone with &quot;Hercules strenght&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T08:10:38-07:00","id":1493976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493975#post1493975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imho, it's like those old urban legends about mothers lifting cars to save their babies in an &quot;adrenaline rush&quot;.<br /> <br /> ...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tought those legends were about the mother sligthly lifting part of a car, not lifting one overhead (and maybe throwing it) like the Hulk, or a vampire with high levels of Potence, would...<br /> <br /> There's a matter of scale to consider here. I would gladly give a reduction of the difficulty of &quot;Feats of Strength&quot; with that argument, but not Potence's full package<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> If you want to &quot;instantly evolve&quot; a superhuman, with superstrength, using Entropy 4, I would say it should require a <i>lot </i>of successes (so, it ain't going to be so instant, not really).<br /> <br /> And that's being generous...It's a lot similar to the argument of replacing Matter with Forces because matter it's energy at a subatomic level...typically the answer to that it's *no*, or make it to be so hard that at the end of the day it's a *no* in disguise<br /> <br /> And even allowing it, it woulnd't have to be Potence <i>per se</i>. Just more Str like if you were using Life 3 sounds legit to me. If you're wanting to emulate the level of <i>reliability </i>that Potence has, it would be <i>legit </i>to say that the creature just has -3 to it's difficulties on that Attribute rolls rather than succeses ... altrough I, personaly, would be more flexible with that last part","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-29-2022, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T08:23:44-07:00","id":1494138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1492980-m20-entropy-sphere-partially-substituting-life?p=1493976#post1493976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tought those legends were about the mother sligthly lifting part of a car, not lifting one overhead (and maybe throwing it) like the Hulk, or a vampire with high levels of Potence, would...<br /> <br /> There's a matter of scale to consider here. I would gladly give a reduction of the difficulty of &amp;quot;Feats of Strength&amp;quot; with that argument, but not Potence's full package<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> If you want to &amp;quot;instantly evolve&amp;quot; a superhuman, with superstrength, using Entropy 4, I would say it should require a <i>lot </i>of successes (so, it ain't going to be so instant, not really).<br /> <br /> And that's being generous...It's a lot similar to the argument of replacing Matter with Forces because matter it's energy at a subatomic level...typically the answer to that it's *no*, or make it to be so hard that at the end of the day it's a *no* in disguise<br /> <br /> And even allowing it, it woulnd't have to be Potence <i>per se</i>. Just more Str like if you were using Life 3 sounds legit to me. If you're wanting to emulate the level of <i>reliability </i>that Potence has, it would be <i>legit </i>to say that the creature just has -3 to it's difficulties on that Attribute rolls rather than succeses ... altrough I, personaly, would be more flexible with that last part</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, mothers saving babies arent awaken mages.<br /> <br /> I do agree that there is a scale to consider here, which is exactly why I would like to have this discussion. The limits of Entropy are indeed hard to set on stone, and ultimately each ST will have to see what is avaiable and pick what they like.<br /> <br /> Bestowing &quot;Hercules strenght&quot; or creating a Captain America super soldier serum indeed is not a quick and dirty trick. Most likely, any such effect would probably temporary; a permanent &quot;blessing&quot; or &quot;genetic engineering&quot; of such super powers obviously follow the rules for successes and duration. I'd say no less than 10 successes per &quot;dot of 'Potence' or 'Fortitude' &quot; gained that way, and that just as a starting point, in case you truly want to make it permanent. And then of course, there's the permadox.<br /> <br /> I do have my own house rules to deal with this specific case of &quot;potence-like&quot; and &quot;fortitude-like&quot; uses of Entropy 4, but each ST would have to choose their own in case they decide to go with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}